"A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>JP 02056294       U</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANEFUSA KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAI TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEFUSA KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAI, TAKAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAI TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAI, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A damping plate capable of suppressing a production cost to a low level and eliminating a dislocation from occurring on a substrate starting with a cracking even if an external force is applied to it from a side direction, wherein a linear bead part (24) is formed at a specified part of a metal plate (10) so as to provide a damping effect to the metal plate (10) by a cracking (26) caused in the bead part (24) and, in the steel plate (10) large in hardening capability, a linear hardened part (28) is formed at a specified part of the steel plate (10) so as to provide a damping effect to the steel plate (10) by a cracking (30) caused in the hardened part (28).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p> La présente invention concerne une plaque d'amortissement permettant de réduire le coût de production et d'éliminer le risque de dislocation pouvant se produire sur un substrat et commençant par une fissure, même si une force externe est appliquée sur le substrat en question dans le sens latéral. On forme un renflement linéaire (24) sur une partie spécifique de la plaque métallique (10) de manière à créer un effet d'amortissement sur la plaque métallique (10) au moyen d'une fissure (26) provoquée dans le renflement (24), et on forme dans la plaque en acier (10) présentant de grandes capacités de durcissement une partie linéaire durcie (28) au niveau d'une partie spécifique de la plaque en acier (10), de manière à créer un effet d'amortissement sur la plaque en acier (10), au moyen d'une fissure (30) provoquée dans la partie durcie (28).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>